        explanation: "OGCR Section I.B.8 states that when the same condition is described as both acute and chronic, AND separate subentries exist at the same indentation level in the Alphabetic Index, you must code BOTH and sequence the ACUTE code FIRST. J03.90 (acute) is sequenced before J35.01 (chronic).",
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="80" font-family="Arial" font-size="38" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">Quiz: Acute on Chronic</text><rect x="100" y="150" width="900" height="220" rx="14" fill="#6366f1"/><text x="550" y="200" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Scenario</text><text x="550" y="245" font-family="Arial" font-size="20" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Dx: Acute and chronic tonsillitis</text><text x="550" y="290" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">Index: acute → J03.90 | chronic → J35.01</text><text x="550" y="325" font-family="Arial" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Same indentation → I.B.8 triggers</text><rect x="100" y="420" width="900" height="200" rx="14" fill="#10b981"/><text x="550" y="470" font-family="Arial" font-size="24" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Correct Answer</text><text x="550" y="520" font-family="Arial" font-size="30" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle">J03.90 → J35.01</text><text x="550" y="575" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Acute first, then chronic</text><rect x="100" y="660" width="900" height="330" rx="14" fill="#ffffff"/><text x="550" y="710" font-family="Arial" font-size="22" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a1a2e" text-anchor="middle">Why?</text><text x="140" y="760" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" fill="#1a1a2e">• OGCR I.B.8: code BOTH when both subentries exist</text><text x="140" y="800" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" fill="#1a1a2e">• Sequence the ACUTE code FIRST (always)</text><text x="140" y="840" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" fill="#1a1a2e">• Requires parallel Index subentries at same indentation</text><text x="140" y="885" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" fill="#ef4444">✗ Chronic-first wrong: contradicts I.B.8 explicit order</text><text x="140" y="925" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" fill="#ef4444">✗ Single-code answers ignore the documentation of both</text><text x="140" y="965" font-family="Arial" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" fill="#6366f1">A single code is never acute AND chronic simultaneously</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Acute first, chronic second — the canonical I.B.8 sequence."
        }
