        content: `**Scenario**: A 78-year-old with a dual-chamber pacemaker placed 9 years ago presents for **elective pulse generator replacement** due to elective replacement indicator (ERI). The surgeon opens the left infraclavicular pocket, disconnects the **existing atrial and ventricular leads**, removes the depleted generator, tests both leads (capture thresholds normal), connects the **new dual-chamber generator**, and closes.

**Wrong code**: 33208 (dual chamber pacemaker insertion). This describes a NEW system with new leads.

**Correct code**: **33228** — "Removal of permanent pacemaker pulse generator with replacement of pacemaker pulse generator; dual lead system."

The leads were **not** replaced — they were tested and reconnected. Only the generator was swapped. Use 33228 (dual lead generator replacement), not 33208. If the patient had a CRT device (3 leads), the answer would be **33229**. ICDs follow the same logic with 33262/33263/33264.`,
