      {
        type: "application",
        title: "The Lab Coder's Decision Tree",
        content: `Build a **lab coding decision tree** for every order. **(1) Does it fit a panel?** Check 80047-80081 — if all components are documented as performed, use the panel code (80048 BMP, 80053 CMP, 80076 Hepatic). Missing even one means **code individually**. **(2) Is it a drug screen?** Distinguish **presumptive (80305-80307)** — simple positive/negative — from **definitive (80320-80377)** — quantitative confirmation. **(3) Was it CLIA-waived in office?** Append **-QW** (81002 UA dipstick, 87880 rapid strep, 82962 fingerstick glucose). **(4) Was it a same-day repeat for trending?** Append **-91**. **(5) Was it sent to a reference lab?** Append **-90**. **(6) Anatomic pathology specimen?** Match the level **88302-88309** to specimen complexity. Run this tree on every requisition and your lab claims will pass audit consistently.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="55" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="34" font-weight="bold">Lab Coding Decision Tree</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="940" height="140" rx="14" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.85"/><text x="130" y="155" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">1.</text><text x="180" y="155" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Panel?</text><text x="180" y="190" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">All components done --&gt; panel code</text><text x="180" y="225" fill="#ffd700" font-size="18">80048 BMP, 80053 CMP, 80076 Hep</text><rect x="80" y="265" width="940" height="140" rx="14" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.85"/><text x="130" y="310" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">2.</text><text x="180" y="310" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Drug screen?</text><text x="180" y="345" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Presumptive 80305-80307 (yes/no)</text><text x="180" y="380" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Definitive 80320-80377 (quantitative)</text><rect x="80" y="420" width="940" height="120" rx="14" fill="#f59e0b" opacity="0.85"/><text x="130" y="465" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">3.</text><text x="180" y="465" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">CLIA-waived in office?</text><text x="180" y="500" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Append -QW (81002, 87880, 82962)</text><rect x="80" y="555" width="940" height="120" rx="14" fill="#ec4899" opacity="0.85"/><text x="130" y="600" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">4.</text><text x="180" y="600" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Same-day repeat?</text><text x="180" y="635" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Append -91 for trending serial results</text><rect x="80" y="690" width="940" height="120" rx="14" fill="#8b5cf6" opacity="0.85"/><text x="130" y="735" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">5.</text><text x="180" y="735" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Sent to reference lab?</text><text x="180" y="770" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Append -90 (you bill, they run)</text><rect x="80" y="825" width="940" height="120" rx="14" fill="#0ea5e9" opacity="0.85"/><text x="130" y="870" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">6.</text><text x="180" y="870" fill="#ffffff" font-size="24" font-weight="bold">Anatomic pathology?</text><text x="180" y="905" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Level 88302-88309 by complexity</text><rect x="80" y="960" width="940" height="80" rx="14" fill="#ffd700"/><text x="550" y="1010" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">Six questions resolve almost every lab claim</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Run the tree on every requisition"
        }
      }
