      {
        type: "application",
        title: "Reading a Path Report to Build the Codes",
        content: `**Your job:** turn a pathology report into a clean claim. Follow this 4-step routine:\n\n**1. Count the specimen containers.** The report header lists each container (often labeled A, B, C). Each container becomes one surgical pathology line.\n**2. Level each specimen.** Look at the **gross description** and the **diagnosis** for each container. Match the organ/biopsy type to the 88300-88309 table.\n**3. Scan for layered services.** Was there a **frozen section** (88331 + 88332)? Were **IHC stains** performed (88342 per antibody)? Was there a **Pap** (88164-88175) or **FNA** (88172/88173)?\n**4. Cross-check NCCI.** Make sure no two codes bundle (e.g., you can't bill 88300 for a specimen you're already billing at 88305).\n\nA disciplined coder catches 6-10 line items where a careless one bills 2. The dollars add up fast.`,
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="70" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="34" font-weight="bold">Path Report → Clean Claim</text><rect x="80" y="130" width="940" height="170" fill="#6366f1" rx="12"/><text x="120" y="170" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Step 1: Count Containers</text><text x="120" y="210" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Header lists A, B, C, ... — each = 1 line</text><text x="120" y="245" fill="#888" font-size="17">Resist the urge to combine</text><text x="120" y="280" fill="#888" font-size="17">Separately submitted = separately billed</text><rect x="80" y="320" width="940" height="170" fill="#10b981" rx="12"/><text x="120" y="360" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Step 2: Level Each</text><text x="120" y="400" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">Gross + diagnosis → 88300/02/04/05/07/09</text><text x="120" y="435" fill="#888" font-size="17">Look up specimen type in the CPT level lists</text><text x="120" y="470" fill="#888" font-size="17">The organ/lesion drives the level</text><rect x="80" y="510" width="940" height="170" fill="#f59e0b" rx="12"/><text x="120" y="550" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Step 3: Layered Services</text><text x="120" y="590" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="20">Frozens: 88331 + 88332</text><text x="120" y="620" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="20">IHC: 88342 per antibody</text><text x="120" y="655" fill="#1a1a2e" font-size="20">Pap (88164-88175) | FNA (88172/88173)</text><rect x="80" y="700" width="940" height="170" fill="#ec4899" rx="12"/><text x="120" y="740" fill="#ffd700" font-size="26" font-weight="bold">Step 4: NCCI Cross-Check</text><text x="120" y="780" fill="#ffffff" font-size="20">No double-billing the same specimen</text><text x="120" y="815" fill="#888" font-size="17">Can't bill 88300 if you also bill 88305 same container</text><text x="120" y="850" fill="#888" font-size="17">Pap method matters — manual vs automated</text><rect x="80" y="890" width="940" height="150" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="3" rx="12"/><text x="550" y="935" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">Discipline = Dollars</text><text x="550" y="975" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Careful reader catches 6-10 line items.</text><text x="550" y="1005" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="18">Careless reader bills 2. Same case. Different claim.</text></svg>`,
          caption: "Four steps from path report to clean claim — disciplined coding catches every line."
        }
      }
